x056 iOS patch: owner view (Bot owner view + hidden agent turns in every conversation)
Rebased by hand on main's ios/ tree (545836f). NOT COMPILED: Swift cannot be built
in the gateway container, so a Mac session must apply it, build and run X056Tests.

  git apply docs/ios-owner-view.patch

Bot (contract docs/bot-owner-view-contract.md):
  - Project.botName / botAttention {needsMe, fyi}; Bot tab shows the name and a badge.
  - BotOrb/Constellation/BotView take the Bot's name.
  - question clearing on session_started only for a human turn (sender nil);
    question_answered handled like question_dismissed; bot_attention, bot_message events.
  - Bot screen filters on the server's botView (+ botLabel "brief"); BotHistory stays
    the fallback for live rows. "For you" / "Needs you" capsules on owner messages.
Every conversation (docs/owner-view-all-contract.md):
  - HistoryEntry: steered, ownerView, ownerTurn, ownerSender, forOwner; Sender: messageId, sessionId.
  - History rows with ownerView "hide" are folded away; live: session_started from
    conversation|mcp|delegate|automation (not this conversation) starts a hidden turn;
    session_done forOwner + triggerMessageId or owner_view un-hides it; errors always show.
  - SystemHistoryToggle is now in More for every conversation with hidden rows
    ("Show N hidden messages"); shown rows are dimmed, agent replies say "reply to <sender>".
  - needsYouCount and settle unread were left as on main (tier none / screenSuppressed
    already skipped).

